---
import {Team}Layout from "../layouts/{Team}Layout.astro";

const pageTitle = "Sources";
const pageTagline = "How {Team} Fan Zone selects, attributes, and checks information.";
---

<{Team}Layout pageTitle={pageTitle} pageTagline={pageTagline} activePath="/sources">
  <section class="sfz-card">
    <h2>Source standards</h2>
    <p>
      The site favors primary sources for team announcements, schedules, transactions, rules, and direct statements.
      Established news organizations and specialist data providers may be used when they offer original reporting or context
      that a primary source does not provide.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sfz-card">
    <h2>Attribution and verification</h2>
    <ul class="sfz-list">
      <li>Article-specific references are listed under “Sources and further reading.”</li>
      <li>Direct quotations and claims originating elsewhere are attributed to their source.</li>
      <li>Reported information is distinguished from {Team} Fan Zone analysis.</li>
      <li>Conflicting or incomplete information is described as uncertain until it can be verified.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="sfz-card">
    <h2>Automated data</h2>
    <p>
      Schedule, score, standings, roster, and statistics pages use structured data refreshed during site builds. Update timing can
      differ from live game coverage. The page timestamp and source note should be used to judge how current a data view is.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sfz-card">
    <h2>Ticket provider coverage</h2>
    <p>The Ticket Finder publishes its connected, listing-level, event-summary, and deep-link-only providers in the on-page Provider coverage section, along with the last successful refresh available in the current snapshot and stale, failed, unmatched-event, or data-granularity limitations. Preview builds use clearly fictional fixture providers and are not evidence of a production connection or commercial relationship.</p>
    <p>Provider descriptions, reviews, guarantees, and FAQs are not copied. Ticket fields are normalized into SFZ's narrower data contract and provider-supplied text is limited to validated plain-text seat and restriction details.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sfz-card">
    <h2>Questions or corrections</h2>
    <p>To question a source or report an error, use the <a href="/contact#corrections">Contact and Corrections page</a> and include the page URL and supporting source.</p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .sfz-card {
      border-radius: 16px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 34, 68, 0.14);
      background: #ffffff;
      padding: 1rem 1.05rem;
      box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
      margin-bottom: 0.95rem;
    }

    .sfz-card h2 {
      margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
      color: var(--navy);
      font-weight: 900;
    }

    .sfz-card p {
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      color: rgba(15, 23, 32, 0.78);
      line-height: 1.6;
      font-weight: 650;
    }

    .sfz-list {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1.2rem;
      color: rgba(15, 23, 32, 0.75);
      line-height: 1.55;
      font-weight: 650;
    }

    .sfz-list li {
      margin: 0.3rem 0;
    }

  </style>
</{Team}Layout>
